Browzy in Chrome
================

This project began as a fork of "Open Claude in Chrome", started by
Sebastian Sosa on 2026-07-21 and licensed under the PolyForm Noncommercial
License 1.0.0 (see LICENSE, which continues to apply).

The current source tree is substantially rewritten. Measured by `git blame`
over the tracked source files (js, mjs, sh, ps1, css, html; excluding
vendored, generated and build output) on the pre-squash history:

    Nguyễn Thế Huy    57,880 lines   71.3%
    Sebastian Sosa    20,965 lines   25.8%
    Al31415            1,718 lines    2.1%
    Rocker Zhang         594 lines    0.7%
                      ------------
                      81,157 lines

The commit history was squashed into a single initial commit on 2026-09-09.
That squash removed the individual commits, not the authorship of the code
those commits contributed — roughly a quarter of the tree above is still the
work of the upstream authors named here, which is why this file exists.

Later work in this repository, including the Browzy rebrand, file
attachments, effort control, prompt enhancement, the slash-dispatch and
session-skills plugin mechanism, provider profile handling and the
installers, is by Nguyễn Thế Huy.

Bundled third-party fonts
-------------------------

The host package ships DejaVu Sans (regular and bold) through the
`dejavu-fonts-ttf` dependency, used to embed a Unicode font in generated PDF
documents — the PDF standard fonts are WinAnsi-encoded and cannot represent
Vietnamese at all. DejaVu Fonts are released under the DejaVu Fonts License,
a free license derived from the Bitstream Vera Fonts Copyright:

    Fonts are (c) Bitstream (see below). DejaVu changes are in public domain.
    Glyphs imported from Arev fonts are (c) Tavmjong Bah (see below).

The full license text ships with the dependency at
`node_modules/dejavu-fonts-ttf/LICENSE`.
